  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Shane Callahan, 50, evening lanes manager at TimberPin Bowling & Cocktail Lanes, was found unresponsive in the cashier counting office on 2018-09-22; manner is homicide from blunt force trauma to the head (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:34–00:34 (doc02), while Shane Callahan's 23:50 outgoing SMS (doc10) narrows the working survival window to 23:50–00:34.\n3. Roman Bell gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 23:00–23:22 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:22 northbound exit and 23:40 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Shane Callahan's 23:50 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Malik Tierney's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2017 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Local keypad memory failed at 23:16 (doc05) and utility interval microfilm (doc11) remains unpulled, leaving narrowed-window access uncorroborated alongside a 2-vs-1 CSI discrepancy, uncollected 23:43 photo, and untested DNA Item 3.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nNo suspect's alibi inside the narrowed 23:50–00:34 window is contradicted yet because local keypad memory failed at 23:16 (doc05). The strongest pre-window conflict is Roman Bell's Year-1 denial vs. ALPR telemetry (resolved in doc08 and cleared of the post-23:50 window by doc09/doc10):\n- doc07: \"I was in Redwood County playing cards with friends from 20:30 until 01:15 and never drove anywhere near TimberPin Bowling & Cocktail Lanes on 2018-09-21.\"\n- doc09: \"2018-09-21 23:00 — US-19 Corridor Gantry Southbound (toward TimberPin Bowling & Cocktail Lanes), plate PEM-5316 (pewter 2017 Hyundai Sonata, reg. Roman Bell).\"\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:50–00:34 (within ME window 22:34–00:34))\n- Vance Mercer: UNCORROBORATED\n- Roman Bell: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Malik Tierney: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Marcus Hargrove: UNCORROBORATED (22:52 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Subpoena and pull the off-site alarm vendor's serial audit backup reel referenced in doc05 covering 23:16 through 00:34 to recover post-battery-fault PIN unlocks.\n2. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for modern STR and touch-DNA profiling.\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Pull unindexed utility microfilm Box referenced in doc11 to obtain 15-minute sub-circuit load strip charts across 22:34–00:34.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Post-23:16 door-access serial backup reel and 15-minute utility sub-meter microfilm were never pulled.\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two torn tamper-evident bank deposit bag stubs observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:43 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
}

