  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Audrey Doyle, 55, second-shift dye-house superintendent at Cumberland Cotton & Dye Works, was found unresponsive in the mezzanine dye-house office on 2018-08-06; manner is homicide from blunt force head injury (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:34–00:34 (doc02), while Audrey Doyle's 23:50 outgoing SMS (doc10) and 23:57 PIN 3512 unlock (doc05) narrow the survival floor to 23:57–00:34.\n3. Arthur Carver gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 23:00–23:22 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:22 northbound exit and 23:40 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Audrey Doyle's 23:50 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Trevor Marsh's departure account shows medium 7-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2017 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Master PIN 9030 (assigned to Dwight Doyle) unlocked the mezzanine dye-house office at 00:11 (doc05) and circuit load ran until 00:23 (doc11), while CSI notes a 2-vs-1 marker 5 discrepancy, an uncollected 23:43 photo, and an unpulled exterior camera.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nDwight Doyle's denial of unlocking or entering the mezzanine dye-house office conflicts with the keypad export:\n- doc03: \"I never entered the mezzanine dye-house office at any point that night. On my rounds I only check the exterior handle from the corridor.\"\n- doc05: \"2018-08-06 00:11 — PIN 9030 UNLOCK\" (paired with doc05 PIN schedule assigning 9030 to Dwight Doyle, and doc11 load drop at 00:23).\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:57–00:34 (within ME window 22:34–00:34))\n- Dwight Doyle: CONTRADICTED\n- Arthur Carver: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Trevor Marsh: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Noah Hendricks: UNCORROBORATED (22:52 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Dwight Doyle in person and ask why master PIN 9030 unlocked the mezzanine dye-house office strike at 00:11 (doc05) while doc03 denies entering and doc04 logs only a corridor handle check.\n2. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Dwight Doyle in person regarding the high-severity contradiction between his 23:00 dark-office claim (doc03) and the AMI sub-meter load continuing until 00:23 (doc11).\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for STR and touch-DNA testing.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two crimped lead bale-lot seals observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:43 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
