  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Denise Espinoza, 56, vault compliance manager at Veritas Clinical Distribution Hub, was found unresponsive in the vault control office on 2015-03-07; manner is homicide from ligature and blunt compressive trauma (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:32–00:32 (doc02), while Denise Espinoza's 23:48 outgoing SMS (doc10) and 23:55 PIN 3632 unlock (doc05) narrow the survival floor to 23:55–00:32.\n3. Cedric Medina gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 22:58–23:20 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:20 northbound exit and 23:38 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Denise Espinoza's 23:48 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Caleb Ibarra's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2014 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Master PIN 9087 (assigned to Marisol Sato) unlocked the vault control office at 00:09 (doc05) and circuit load ran until 00:21 (doc11), while CSI notes a 2-vs-1 marker 5 discrepancy, an uncollected 23:41 photo, and an unpulled exterior camera.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nMarisol Sato's denial of unlocking or entering the vault control office conflicts with the keypad export:\n- doc03: \"I never entered the vault control office at any point that night. On my rounds I only check the exterior handle from the corridor.\"\n- doc05: \"2015-03-07 00:09 — PIN 9087 UNLOCK\" (paired with doc05 PIN schedule assigning 9087 to Marisol Sato, and doc11 load drop at 00:21).\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:55–00:32 (within ME window 22:32–00:32))\n- Marisol Sato: CONTRADICTED\n- Cedric Medina: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Caleb Ibarra: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Sabrina Whitaker: UNCORROBORATED (22:50 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Marisol Sato in person and ask why master PIN 9087 unlocked the vault control office strike at 00:09 (doc05) while doc03 denies entering and doc04 logs only a corridor handle check.\n2. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Marisol Sato in person regarding the high-severity contradiction between his 23:00 dark-office claim (doc03) and the AMI sub-meter load continuing until 00:21 (doc11).\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for STR and touch-DNA testing.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two severed serialized red DEA tote seals observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:41 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
