  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Lucia Villarreal, 39, scale-house settlement manager at Ironworks Metal Recycling & Scale, was found unresponsive in the scale-house settlement office on 2016-06-06; manner is homicide from blunt force cranial trauma (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:36–00:36 (doc02), while Lucia Villarreal's 23:52 outgoing SMS (doc10) and 23:59 PIN 3991 unlock (doc05) narrow the survival floor to 23:59–00:36.\n3. Clint Faulkner gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 23:02–23:24 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:24 northbound exit and 23:42 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Lucia Villarreal's 23:52 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Kenneth Devera's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2015 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Master PIN 9056 (assigned to Celeste Prescott) unlocked the scale-house settlement office at 00:13 (doc05) and circuit load ran until 00:25 (doc11), while CSI notes a 2-vs-1 marker 5 discrepancy, an uncollected 23:45 photo, and an unpulled exterior camera.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nCeleste Prescott's denial of unlocking or entering the scale-house settlement office conflicts with the keypad export:\n- doc03: \"I never entered the scale-house settlement office at any point that night. On my rounds I only check the exterior handle from the corridor.\"\n- doc05: \"2016-06-06 00:13 — PIN 9056 UNLOCK\" (paired with doc05 PIN schedule assigning 9056 to Celeste Prescott, and doc11 load drop at 00:25).\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:59–00:36 (within ME window 22:36–00:36))\n- Celeste Prescott: CONTRADICTED\n- Clint Faulkner: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Kenneth Devera: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Alicia Benitez: UNCORROBORATED (22:54 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Celeste Prescott in person and ask why master PIN 9056 unlocked the scale-house settlement office strike at 00:13 (doc05) while doc03 denies entering and doc04 logs only a corridor handle check.\n2. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Celeste Prescott in person regarding the high-severity contradiction between his 23:00 dark-office claim (doc03) and the AMI sub-meter load continuing until 00:25 (doc11).\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for STR and touch-DNA testing.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two carbon-copy copper weight tickets observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:45 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
