  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Keith Pacheco, 34, night-audit general manager at Pinecrest Motor Lodge, was found unresponsive in the registration night-audit office on 2015-03-16; manner is homicide from two penetrating 9mm gunshot wounds to the chest (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:36–00:36 (doc02), while Keith Pacheco's 23:52 outgoing SMS (doc10) narrows the working survival window to 23:52–00:36.\n3. Brenda Thorne gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 23:02–23:24 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:24 northbound exit and 23:42 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Keith Pacheco's 23:52 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Kirk Carver's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2014 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Local keypad memory failed at 23:18 (doc05) and utility interval microfilm (doc11) remains unpulled, leaving narrowed-window access uncorroborated alongside a 2-vs-1 CSI discrepancy, uncollected 23:45 photo, and untested DNA Item 3.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nNo suspect's alibi inside the narrowed 23:52–00:36 window is contradicted yet because local keypad memory failed at 23:18 (doc05). The strongest pre-window conflict is Brenda Thorne's Year-1 denial vs. ALPR telemetry (resolved in doc08 and cleared of the post-23:52 window by doc09/doc10):\n- doc07: \"I was in Bergen County playing cards with friends from 20:30 until 01:15 and never drove anywhere near Pinecrest Motor Lodge on 2015-03-15.\"\n- doc09: \"2015-03-15 23:02 — Palisades Connector Gantry Southbound (toward Pinecrest Motor Lodge), plate KDL-2361 (white 2015 Ram 1500 Tradesman, reg. Brenda Thorne).\"\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:52–00:36 (within ME window 22:36–00:36))\n- Russell Ingram: UNCORROBORATED\n- Brenda Thorne: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Kirk Carver: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Leon Hendricks: UNCORROBORATED (22:54 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Subpoena and pull the off-site alarm vendor's serial audit backup reel referenced in doc05 covering 23:18 through 00:36 to recover post-battery-fault PIN unlocks.\n2. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for modern STR and touch-DNA profiling.\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Pull unindexed utility microfilm Box referenced in doc11 to obtain 15-minute sub-circuit load strip charts across 22:36–00:36.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Post-23:18 door-access serial backup reel and 15-minute utility sub-meter microfilm were never pulled.\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two spent 9mm brass shell casings observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:45 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
