  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Garrett Quinn, 45, vault compliance manager at MedCore Regional Wholesale Cage, was found unresponsive in the vault control office on 2017-07-22; manner is homicide from ligature and blunt compressive trauma (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:36–00:36 (doc02), while Garrett Quinn's 23:52 outgoing SMS (doc10) and 23:59 PIN 3547 unlock (doc05) narrow the survival floor to 23:59–00:36.\n3. Helena Tierney gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 23:02–23:24 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:24 northbound exit and 23:42 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Garrett Quinn's 23:52 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Alton Molina's departure account shows medium 7-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2016 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Master PIN 9079 (assigned to Lonnie Alvarez) unlocked the vault control office at 00:13 (doc05) and circuit load ran until 00:25 (doc11), while CSI notes a 2-vs-1 marker 5 discrepancy, an uncollected 23:45 photo, and an unpulled exterior camera.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nLonnie Alvarez's denial of unlocking or entering the vault control office conflicts with the keypad export:\n- doc03: \"I never entered the vault control office at any point that night. On my rounds I only check the exterior handle from the corridor.\"\n- doc05: \"2017-07-22 00:13 — PIN 9079 UNLOCK\" (paired with doc05 PIN schedule assigning 9079 to Lonnie Alvarez, and doc11 load drop at 00:25).\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:59–00:36 (within ME window 22:36–00:36))\n- Lonnie Alvarez: CONTRADICTED\n- Helena Tierney: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Alton Molina: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Floyd Briggs: UNCORROBORATED (22:54 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Lonnie Alvarez in person and ask why master PIN 9079 unlocked the vault control office strike at 00:13 (doc05) while doc03 denies entering and doc04 logs only a corridor handle check.\n2. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Lonnie Alvarez in person regarding the high-severity contradiction between his 23:00 dark-office claim (doc03) and the AMI sub-meter load continuing until 00:25 (doc11).\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for STR and touch-DNA testing.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two severed serialized red DEA tote seals observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:45 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
